{"t": "Seminar Details", "b": "<h2 id=\"seminar-details\">Seminar Details</h2>\n<div class=\"cp-card\">\n<p>\n                                        Seminar Title:\n                                    </p>\n<p>\n                                        First Order Gradient Based Methods\n                                    </p>\n<p>\n                                        Seminar Type:\n                                    </p>\n<p>\n                                        Progress Seminar\n                                    </p>\n<p>\n                                        Department:\n                                    </p>\n<p>\n                                        Mathematics\n                                    </p>\n<p>\n                                        Speaker Name:\n                                    </p>\n<p>\n                                        Milan Barik ( Rollno : 523ma2010)\n                                    </p>\n<p>\n                                        Speaker Type:\n                                    </p>\n<p>\n                                        Student\n                                    </p>\n<p>\n                                        Venue:\n                                    </p>\n<p>\n                                        Seminar Room (Department of Mathematics)\n                                    </p>\n<p>\n                                        Date and Time:\n                                    </p>\n<p>\n                                        24 Jun 2026 05.00 PM\n                                    </p>\n<p>\n                                        Contact:\n                                    </p>\n<p>\n                                         Suvendu Ranjan Pattanaik\n                                    </p>\n<p>\n                                        Abstract:\n                                    </p>\n<p>We study accelerated gradient-based methods for composite non-smooth optimization<br/>\nproblems. We establish convergence rates for the objective residual and the subdifferential<br/>\nresidual, and prove the convergence of the generated iterates. By discretizing suitable<br/>\noptimization-related dynamical systems, we derive new algorithms and analyze their<br/>\nconvergence properties. Numerical experiments are conducted to validate the theoretical<br/>\nresults and illustrate the performance of the proposed methods.</p>\n<p>\n<a class=\"cp-off\" href=\"https://www.nitrkl.ac.in/Research/PrintSeminar/?id=CfDJ8ITBfTALY3BEiHl9qNgHje2g6RM_ZY1-7rR3SeFWZoXh628DTBwd_Zx9dOsnAedUMJqEZ4tw6x3tQVKJbfkQnaZ12FNcIf_Dy_KBh5gZZGOH2mchwa-lsJr2lZQfnjWr1w\" title=\"Print Seminar\"> Print Seminar</a>\n</p>\n</div>", "u": "https://www.nitrkl.ac.in/MA/ViewSeminar/?id=CfDJ8ITBfTALY3BEiHl9qNgHje159WdahUhL0CuYDayD3uJbk5yVkNQgaWt-U0NJOWusBx1oMm2KBB4J5inXoPO2HWRh1sVY1MZWHCuVU_WhIuhskQt0N1e9nNpILkOgqrsoYA"}